# Replace `FolderItem.type` with `FolderItem.kind`

## Problem

Adding a new system folder (like "Home") requires touching 5+ files:
- `systemFolders` data array
- `resolveKind()` — hardcoded ID check
- `resolveChildIds()` — potentially a new case
- `folderTree.ts` — `type !== 'system'` guards
- `noteService.ts` — `type === 'system'` redirect
- `noteListView.svelte.ts` — `type !== 'system'` check

The root cause: `type: 'system'` is a meaningless catch-all. `resolveKind()` then re-derives meaning from IDs.

## Solution

`FolderItem` gets a `kind` field that IS the profile key. `PROFILE_REGISTRY` is already the single source of truth for capabilities. All downstream code reads `kind` instead of `type`.

**Adding a new system folder becomes:** add item to `systemFolders` with the right `kind` + add profile to `PROFILE_REGISTRY`. Done.

---

## Changes

### 1. Data Layer: `folders.svelte.ts`

#### Replace `FolderType` with `SidebarKind`

```typescript
// BEFORE
export type FolderType = 'all' | 'trash' | 'regular' | 'system';
type?: FolderType;

// AFTER
import type { SidebarKind } from '$lib/views/folderSidebarView.svelte';
kind?: SidebarKind;
```

> [!WARNING]
> **Circular dependency risk.** `SidebarKind` is currently defined in the view layer. Since the data layer needs it, we must move `SidebarKind` to a shared location — either `folders.svelte.ts` itself or a new `types.ts`.
>
> **Proposed**: Define `SidebarKind` in `folders.svelte.ts` (it's a data concept — what kind of folder this is). The view imports it from there.

#### Update `systemFolders`

```typescript
const systemFolders: FolderItem[] = [
    { id: 'deleted-notes', title: 'Recently Deleted', kind: 'trash', ... },
    { id: 'favorites',     title: 'Favorites',        kind: 'favorites', ... },
    { id: 'home',          title: 'Home',              kind: 'home', ... }
];
```

#### Update `trashItems` derived

```diff
- if (folder.type !== 'trash' && folder.deletedAt != null) {
+ if (folder.kind !== 'trash' && folder.deletedAt != null) {
```

#### Update `getDefaultFolderId()`

```diff
- if (!folder.type || folder.type === 'regular') return folder.id;
+ if (!folder.kind || folder.kind === 'regular') return folder.id;
```

---

### 2. View Layer: `folderSidebarView.svelte.ts`

#### Move `SidebarKind` export to `folders.svelte.ts`

Remove `export type SidebarKind = ...` from here. Import it from `folders.svelte`.

#### Simplify `resolveKind()`

```typescript
// BEFORE — 5 lines of branching, hardcoded IDs
private resolveKind(item: FolderItem): SidebarKind {
    if (item.deletedAt != null) return 'deleted';
    if (item.type === 'trash') return 'trash';
    if (item.id === 'favorites') return 'favorites';
    if (item.id === 'home') return 'home';
    return 'regular';
}

// AFTER — 2 lines, no ID checks
private resolveKind(item: FolderItem): SidebarKind {
    if (item.deletedAt != null) return 'deleted';
    return item.kind ?? 'regular';
}
```

#### Add Home child resolution in `resolveChildIds()`

Home surfaces folders with `parentId === null` (excluding other view-kind folders):

```typescript
private resolveChildIds(kind: SidebarKind, item: FolderItem): FolderID[] {
    switch (kind) {
        case 'trash':
            return this.folderQueries.getTrashRootIds();
        case 'favorites':
            return this.folderQueries.getFavoriteFolderIds();
        case 'home':
            return this.folderQueries.getHomeFolderChildIds();
        case 'deleted':
            return [];
        default:
            return item.items ?? [];
    }
}
```

#### Update `noteCount` line in `buildSource()`

```diff
- noteCount: this.noteQueries.getNoteCountForFolder(item.id, item.type),
+ noteCount: this.noteQueries.getNoteCountForFolder(item.id, item.kind),
```

---

### 3. Domain Layer: `folderTree.ts`

#### `getFavoriteFolderIds()` — exclude non-regular folders

```diff
- folder.type !== 'trash' && folder.type !== 'system'
+ !folder.kind || folder.kind === 'regular'
```

This reads: "only regular user folders can be favorites" — which is what the check always meant.

#### `collectActiveFolderIds()` — exclude system/trash

```diff
- if (!folder || folder.type === 'trash' || folder.type === 'system' || folder.deletedAt != null) return;
+ if (!folder || (folder.kind && folder.kind !== 'regular') || folder.deletedAt != null) return;
```

#### `getNotesForFolder()` — trash folder note listing

```diff
- } else if (folderId === 'deleted-notes') {
+ } else if (folderKind === 'trash') {
```

The `folderType` parameter becomes `folderKind?: SidebarKind`. When `kind === 'trash'`, show deleted notes. When `kind === 'home'`, show notes with `folderId === null`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Home note listing**: When the Home folder is selected, `getNotesForFolder` should return notes with `folderId === null`. This is the same as the current `folderId === null` / `'root'` path. We just need `folderKind === 'home'` to trigger it.

```typescript
if (folderKind === 'trash') {
    resultNotes = allNotes.filter((note) => note.deletedAt != null);
} else if (folderKind === 'home') {
    resultNotes = allNotes.filter(
        (note) => note.folderId == null && note.deletedAt == null
    );
} else { ... }
```

#### Add `getHomeFolderChildIds()` method

```typescript
getHomeFolderChildIds(): FolderID[] {
    return this.folders.items.filter((id) => {
        const folder = this.folders.findItemById(id);
        return folder && (!folder.kind || folder.kind === 'regular') && folder.deletedAt == null;
    });
}
```

This returns top-level regular folders — i.e., the user's actual folder tree. These show as children under Home in the sidebar.

